90: rows = []
91: 
92: def row(name, got, want, note=""):
93:     assert name not in [n for n, _ in rows], "DUPLICATE ROW NAME %r" % name
94:     assert len(name) <= 15, name    # load-bearing for gate_arm.sh: `%-16s' plus a literal space keep its `^$v  .*ok$' pattern satisfiable (pass 9, Opus)
95:     ok = (got == want)
96:     rows.append((name, ok))
97:     print("%-16s %-12s %-12s %-46s %s" % (name, str(got), str(want), note,
98:                                           "ok" if ok else "FAIL"))
99:     return ok
100: 
101: def session(cmds, settle=1.5, spin=1.2):
299: #  minimax's NON-SUPPRESSING mutant (announce correctly, then forget `assert = 0') is NOT covered
300: #  by any row here.
301: #
302: #  *** DO NOT USE THE `IPL ... => ASSERT' debug LINE AS THE ORACLE.  It is the obvious candidate and
303: #  it is WRONG, for a reason that has nothing to do with visibility. ***
304: #
305: #  `debug("[ pcc2: IPL = %i, MASK = %i => %s ]")' sits at the FOOT of reassert_interrupts() but
306: #  EXECUTES BEFORE BOTH SUPPRESSIONS -- the MIEN test and the C040 test are BELOW it, and only the
307: #  INTERRUPT_ASSERT/DEASSERT pair after them reflects the real line state.  Verified by line order.
308: #  So the message reports the PRE-SUPPRESSION value of `assert' and is green under the very mutant it
309: #  would be chosen to catch.  *Named by the codex seat on pass 1: "do not use the existing
310: #  `IPL ... => ASSERT' debug message as the line-state oracle: it executes before MIEN suppression
311: #  and before the proposed C040 suppression.  Observe the interrupt callback/state."*
312: #
313: #  (Two earlier drafts of this paragraph were wrong in two different ways.  The first said the line
314: #  was ABSENT at default verbosity -- false; it prints while single-stepping, and the "0 occurrences"
315: #  came from grepping the probe's own STDOUT ARTIFACT instead of the captured pty text.  The second
316: #  then proposed it as the oracle.  **Visibility was never the question; POSITION was.**)
317: #
318: #  *** WHAT ACTUALLY BLOCKS THE ROW IS THAT ITS CHANNEL CANNOT VARY, AND THAT IS A SOURCE FACT. ***
319: #  For the tail to print ASSERT at all, some interrupt must be pending above the mask -- i.e. an
320: #  INT bit set in one of the ICRs.  MEASURED by reading every guest-writable arm: TxICR keeps only
321: #  `idata & 0x17' and SCCICR only `idata & 0x1f', so PCC2_IRQ_INT (0x20) is MASKED OUT OF EVERY
322: #  WRITABLE ARM.  The bit's only producer is reassert_interrupts() itself, from
323: #  pending_timerN_interrupts, which are incremented by the TIMER TICK -- and a stepped probe cannot
324: #  run one, because the debugger stops host-timer callbacks for the duration of `step'.
325: #
326: #  So this is the accept-row failability rule one level up: a NEVER-SET-BY-GUEST bit cannot carry
327: #  the row, and no amount of verbosity changes that.  The row needs a FREE-RUNNING probe shape.
328: #
329: #  *** AND IT IS A MEASURED ESCAPE, NOT A PREDICTED ONE.  KILL TABLE, 2026-09-08, artifacts in
330: #  regress/artifacts/pcc2c040kill/killtable_20260907/: ***
331: #
332: #      BASE                                   7/7
333: #      M_b_reinstate   the verbatim exit(1)   3/7   floor (b) -- KILLED
334: #      M_d2_silent     announce deleted       4/7   floor (d) -- KILLED
335: #      M_d3_nolatch    announce every call    6/7   floor (d) -- KILLED (c040 once, scores 2)
336: #      M_d4_collide    latch bit reused       6/7   floor (d) -- KILLED (c040 predirty)
337: #      M_d1_noassert   `assert = 0' removed   7/7   *** ESCAPES -- CLEAN SWEEP ***
338: #
339: #  *** THIS IS A FLOOR BREACH UNDER CLAUSE (d), AND THIS FILE DOES NOT PRETEND OTHERWISE. ***
340: #  `assert = 0' IS the repair's effect, so removing it is (d)'s canonical "keep the guard, null the
341: #  repair" -- inside the DEPENDS-ON closure, not outside it.  Calling it clause-(e) contract debt
342: #  would be using the contract as an escape hatch, which is the one thing clause (e) must not become.
343: #
344: #  THE CONTRACT, stated honestly: this detector catches REINSTATEMENT of the host kill, a SILENT
345: #  decline, a NON-LATCHING announce and a COLLIDING latch bit -- all four MEASURED.  It does NOT
346: #  catch a fix that announces correctly and fails to suppress the assertion.  The repair for that is
347: #  a free-running probe (breakpoint + `continue', so host-timer callbacks run and a timer interrupt
348: #  can go pending), which is a different probe shape rather than another row here.
349: 
350: #  ================================================================================================
351: #  #512 L2 REPAIR -- the non-suppressing mutant, which the seven rows above CANNOT see.
352: #
353: #  MEASURED: removing `assert = 0' scores 7/7 (killtable_20260907/M_d1_noassert.raw), and a pass-2
354: #  seat named a ONE-TOKEN variant, `assert = 0;' -> `return;', that also scores 7/7.
355: #
356: #  *** THE DESIGN BELOW IS A REVISION.  MY FIRST ONE WOULD HAVE PASSED THE `return' MUTANT. ***
357: #  The codex design review (artifacts/pcc2c040kill/codex_assertrow_20260908.txt) found why:
358: #
359: #      GENCTL resets to ZERO, so MIEN is clear through the setup and every recalculation DEASSERTS
360: #      the CPU line.  At the final write the repair deasserts (no interrupt), deleting `assert = 0'
361: #      asserts (caught) -- but `return' LEAVES THE ALREADY-DEASSERTED LINE UNCHANGED, so it also
362: #      shows no interrupt and PASSES.  *"Deleting the assignment permits assertion; returning
363: #      preserves the incoming line state."*
364: #
365: #  THE FIX IS A PRECONDITION, NOT AN ORACLE: both rows write MIEN-ONLY GENCTL FIRST, so the line is
366: #  ALREADY ASSERTED before the operation under test.  Then `return' leaves it asserted and reddens.
367: #
368: #  AND THE OBVIOUS ORACLE IS A CHECK THAT CANNOT FAIL: rd() tests `until in buf' against the WHOLE
369: #  accumulated transcript, and the settle drain has already buffered a `GXemul>' prompt -- so
370: #  ("continue", grace, "GXemul>") returns True with ZERO READS.  `how == "no-breakpoint"' is no
371: #  better: it proves a MISSING TOKEN, not execution-without-delivery, and a hang satisfies it.
372: #  So BOTH rows stop at a breakpoint and the discriminator is WHICH PC, never a timeout.
373: #  ================================================================================================
374: 
375: IRQ_ENTRY = 0x8        #  m88k EXCEPTION_INTERRUPT is vector 1; entry = VBR + 8*vector, and VBR is
376:                        #  0 because mvmeprom.c EXPLICITLY sets it -- not an assumed reset value.
377: STCR_R5_CR1 = 0x80058025   #  stcr r5,cr1 -- copied from m88k_exc_probe.py and decoder-checked by
378:                            #  the review, NOT hand-assembled (the encoding trap this project records)
379: PSR_INDCLR = 0x80000000    #  MODE only, IND CLEAR: dispatch needs `irq_asserted && !(PSR & IND)'
380: CLMPCC = 0xfff45000
381: CLMPCC_IER = 0x11
382: SCCTX_ARM = 0x13       #  PCC2_IRQ_IEN | level 3.  The device ORs in INT (0x20) -> 0x33; MASK
383:                        #  resets to 0, so IPL 3 wins the comparison.
384: IER_ON = 0x03          #  clmpcc asserts SCC TX when (IER & 3) != 0
385: 
386: 
387: def ST_B7(rs, off):    #  store via r7 (the clmpcc base); ST_B is hardwired to r2 (PCC2)
388:     return enc(0x0b, rs, 7, off)
389: 
390: 
391: def assert_row(label, final_genctl, repeat=1, then_genctl=None):
392:     #  Setup runs under `step' -- dispatch is suppressed while single-stepping BY DESIGN, so the
393:     #  line can be armed without the interrupt being taken early.
394:     insns = [
395:         STCR_R5_CR1,               # 0  PSR: interrupts enabled
396:         ST_B(6, SCCTX),            # 1  SCCTX = 0x13   (IEN | level 3)
397:         ST_B7(8, CLMPCC_IER),      # 2  clmpcc IER -> INTERRUPT_ASSERT(irq_scc_tx), synchronous
398:         LD_BU(11, SCCTX),          # 3  read back: must be 0x33, proving INT arrived
399:         ST_B(9, GENCTL),           # 4  MIEN only -- THE PRECONDITION: the line is now ASSERTED
400:     ] + [ST_B(10, GENCTL)] * repeat  # 5..  the operation under test, ONCE or TWICE
401:     if then_genctl is not None:      # ..  and optionally a FOLLOWING write (the recovery cell)
402:         insns = insns + [ST_B(13, GENCTL)]
403:     #  COLLATERAL-STATE readback, costing NO extra session: three seats independently named
404:     #  suppression-by-clobbering (codex "collateral state changes"; grok `GENCTL &= ~PCC2_MIEN';
405:     #  deepseek "replace `assert = 0' with `MIEN = 0' -- the rows check only that no interrupt is
406:     #  delivered, they do not check that MIEN remains set").  Read GENCTL back so a fix that
407:     #  suppresses by disabling ALL interrupts is visible.
408:     insns = insns + [LD_BU(14, GENCTL)]
409: 
410:     #  6 is a harmless RAM store (I_ST_SCR = st r5,r3,0, already defined by the scaffolding) purely
411:     #  so the COMPLETION breakpoint at 7 is an address the guest ARRIVES AT rather than one it is
412:     #  already sitting on after `step'.  Do NOT hand-assemble an instruction here: `enc()' builds
413:     #  the IMMEDIATE form, and a triadic register op needs a different encoder.
414:     words = insns + [I_ST_SCR, I_BR_SELF, 0]     # harmless, then br . = COMPLETION
415:     #  DERIVED, never hardcoded: `repeat' changes the instruction count, and a stale literal here
416:     #  would put the completion breakpoint on the wrong word and make the row unfalsifiable.
417:     completion = CODE + 4 * (len(insns) + 1)
418:     cmds = ["put w 0x%x, 0x%08x" % (CODE + 4 * i, w) for i, w in enumerate(words)]
419:     cmds += ["put w 0x%x, 0x%08x" % (IRQ_ENTRY, I_BR_SELF)]     # the vector spins, not zeros
420:     cmds += ["r2=0x%x" % PCC2, "r5=0x%x" % PSR_INDCLR, "r6=0x%x" % SCCTX_ARM,
421:              "r7=0x%x" % CLMPCC, "r8=0x%x" % IER_ON, "r9=0x02",
422:              "r10=0x%x" % final_genctl, "r11=0x0", "r12=0x0",
423:              "r13=0x%x" % (then_genctl if then_genctl is not None else 0)]
424:     cmds += ["breakpoint add 0x%x" % IRQ_ENTRY,
425:              "breakpoint add 0x%x" % completion]
426:     cmds += ["pc=0x%x" % CODE, "step %d" % len(insns),
427:              ("continue", 6.0), "reg"]
428:     t, alive, how = session(cmds, spin=2.0)
429:     pcs = re.findall(r"pc\s*=\s*0x([0-9a-f]{8})", t)
430:     r11 = re.findall(r"r11\s*=\s*0x([0-9a-f]+)", t)
431:     r14 = re.findall(r"r14\s*=\s*0x([0-9a-f]+)", t)
432:     return (t, alive, how, (int(pcs[-1], 16) if pcs else None),
433:             (int(r11[-1], 16) if r11 else None), completion,
434:             (int(r14[-1], 16) if r14 else None))
435: 
436: #  ---- LIVENESS + POSITIVE CONTROL: with C040 CLEAR the interrupt MUST be delivered -------------
437: tc, alivec, howc, pcc, r11c, compc, gc = assert_row("live", 0x02)
438: 
439: row("irq pending", ("0x%02x" % r11c) if r11c is not None else "no-readback", "0x33",
440:     "LIVENESS: the clmpcc IER store must set SCCTX's INT bit -- without this the pair is vacuous")
441: 
442: row("irq live", ("0x%x" % pcc) if pcc is not None else "no-pc(%s)" % howc, "0x%x" % IRQ_ENTRY,
443:     "POSITIVE CONTROL: C040 CLEAR, line asserted -- the interrupt vector MUST be reached")
444: 
445: #  ---- THE DEFECT ROW: same sequence, C040 SET -- delivery must be suppressed --------------------
446: #  Affirmative negative evidence: it must REACH THE COMPLETION BREAKPOINT, not merely fail to
447: #  reach the vector.  A timeout, an unexpected stop or a death is a FAILURE, never the answer.
448: td, alived, howd, pcd, r11d, compd, gd = assert_row("c040", 0x06)
449: 
450: row("c040 noassert", ("0x%x" % pcd) if pcd is not None else "no-pc(%s)" % howd,
451:     "0x%x" % compd,
452:     "C040 SET on an ALREADY-ASSERTED line: must reach completion, NOT the interrupt vector")
453: 
454: #  ---- THE SECOND ENCOUNTER.  This closes the ENCOUNTER axis rather than chasing one mutant. -----
455: #  MEASURED: with only the row above, `assert = 0' moved INSIDE the latch scores 10/10
456: #  (killtable_20260908/M_latchinside.raw).  It suppresses correctly on the FIRST C040 encounter --
457: #  the latch is unset, so the body runs -- and skips the suppression on EVERY LATER ONE.  The codex
458: #  pass-1 seat predicted exactly this: *"The first encounter suppresses correctly; later encounters
459: #  can assert the CPU line.  The announcement count remains exactly one."*
460: #
461: #  The axis has two cells, FIRST and LATER, and the rows above held only the first.  A second
462: #  identical C040 write closes it: under the shipped fix `assert = 0' is outside the latch and runs
463: #  both times; under the mutant the second call leaves the line asserted and the interrupt lands.
464: t2, alive2b, how2b, pc2b, r112b, comp2b, g2b = assert_row("c040x2", 0x06, repeat=2)
465: 
466: row("c040 noassert2", ("0x%x" % pc2b) if pc2b is not None else "no-pc(%s)" % how2b,
467:     "0x%x" % comp2b,
468:     "the SECOND C040 encounter, latch already set, must ALSO suppress -- the encounter axis")
469: 
470: #  ---- THE FOURTH CELL: RECOVERY.  C040 CLEARED after the latch has fired. -----------------------
471: #  *** THE THREE ROWS ABOVE DO NOT CLOSE THE AXIS, and calling it closed was this round's SECOND
472: #  attempt to grade a floor-shaped hole as contract debt. ***  The C040 block reads TWO device-state
473: #  lvalues -- `GENCTL & PCC2_C040' and `warned & (1u << PCC2_W_C040)' -- so their product is FOUR
474: #  cells, not two (grok, pass 2 on the L2 repair):
475: #
476: #                    warned = 0            warned = 1
477: #      C040 clear    `irq live'            *** THIS ROW ***
478: #      C040 set      `c040 noassert'       `c040 noassert2'
479: #
480: #  `irq live' does NOT hold the empty cell: it runs on a FRESH machine, so `warned' is 0.  It is the
481: #  accept row for C040-clear, not for C040-clear-AFTER-C040-set.
482: #
483: #  THE MUTANT IT KILLS, named by the same seat -- STICKY SUPPRESSION, one line:
484: #      if ((GENCTL & PCC2_C040) || (d->warned & (1u << PCC2_W_C040))) {
485: #  After the first C040 write `warned' is set, so every later call zeros `assert' even with C040
486: #  CLEAR.  Predicted to score 11/11 against the rows above -- a clean sweep -- because every one of
487: #  them either runs fresh or keeps C040 set.
488: t3, alive3b, how3b, pc3b, r113b, comp3b, g3b = assert_row("c040rec", 0x06, then_genctl=0x02)
489: 
490: row("c040 recover", ("0x%x" % pc3b) if pc3b is not None else "no-pc(%s)" % how3b,
491:     "0x%x" % IRQ_ENTRY,
492:     "C040 CLEARED after the latch fired: assertion must RESUME -- the fourth product cell")
493: 
494: #  ---- COLLATERAL STATE: suppression must not be achieved by CLOBBERING. -------------------------
495: #  THREE SEATS named this independently on pass 2 and no row saw it: codex called it "collateral
496: #  state changes"; grok named `assert = 0;' plus `GENCTL &= ~PCC2_MIEN'; deepseek put it as
497: #  *"replace `assert = 0' with `MIEN = 0' -- the rows check only that no interrupt is DELIVERED,
498: #  they do not check that MIEN remains SET.  Suppression by masking passes every row."*
499: #
500: #  Costs NO extra session: the readback rides on the sessions already run.  GENCTL must still read
501: #  back what the guest wrote -- MIEN set, C040 set -- after the suppression has happened.
502: row("c040 genctl", ("0x%02x" % gd) if gd is not None else "no-readback", "0x06",
503:     "GENCTL must read back MIEN|C040: suppression by clobbering MIEN would pass every other row")
504: 
505: #  ---- THE LIVENESS CONTROL WAS ONLY APPLIED TO ONE SESSION OF FOUR. ----------------------------
506: #  Named by the kimi-k3:cloud seat on pass 2: *"assert_row() returns r11d and r112b, and no row
507: #  checks them.  Disposition 3 is correct but INCOMPLETELY APPLIED.  Its own rationale -- 'no
508: #  interrupt' must be distinguishable from 'no request was ever created' -- applies with equal force
509: #  to the two C040 sessions, yet the request check exists only for the live session."*
510: #
511: #  It is exactly right, and it is the vacuity shape: `c040 noassert' reaching COMPLETION is
512: #  consistent with "the fix suppressed correctly" AND with "no interrupt was ever pending in that
513: #  session".  Only the SCCTX readback separates them.  Free -- the sessions already ran.
514: for _lbl, _v in (("c040 pending", r11d), ("c040x2 pending", r112b), ("c040rec pending", r113b)):
515:     row(_lbl, ("0x%02x" % _v) if _v is not None else "no-readback", "0x33",
516:         "LIVENESS for THIS session: without it, `completion' cannot be told from `never asked'")
517: 
518: ok = sum(1 for _, o in rows if o)
519: print("")
520: print("PCC2C040_RESULT=%d/%d" % (ok, len(rows)))
521: print("PCC2C040_WITNESS=%s" % ("PASS" if ok == len(rows) else "FAIL"))
522: print("PCC2C040_DONE")

