| Set | Set | `c040 noassert2` | Completion PC rather than interrupt entry. |
| Clear | Set | `c040 recover` | Interrupt-entry PC rather than completion. |

That table describes **delivery checks in the supplied fixtures**, not coverage of every read-set partition or every possible change within those four projected cells.

The announcement rows observe a different effect. The pending rows validate a request readback taken during setup; they do not independently observe the eventual delivery decision. The GENCTL row observes retained register state. These properties cannot be substituted for one another when deciding whether an oracle holds a cell.

The source establishes these comparisons; I did not execute the detector or measure additional counterfactual edits.

**Q4.** I’m not supplying the requested guest-triggerable-gap classification. There is also an evidentiary limit: the permitted device-code portions do not establish every input’s producer, so they cannot justify an exhaustive claim that some state is impossible through guest activity.

In particular, **not directly writable** does not mean **unreachable through guest-caused device activity**. Neither omission from these fixtures nor absence of a writer from the inspected function is sufficient evidence for assigning an obligation to disclosed debt.
